{"records":[{"id":"h772d6cx3f","title":"SynLethDB-Recon3D-A549","description":"The datasets associated with the article “Metabolic Synthetic Lethality–Guided Drug Repurposing for Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer: An Integrated Systems Biology and Molecular Modeling Study” are provided in three separate files, each corresponding to a distinct stage of the study.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-05-26T11:56:09.523Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/h772d6cx3f","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/h772d6cx3f"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sonia","last_name":"Sepahi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Computational Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fkbrcn84vz","title":"Integrating proteomics and metabolomics to reveal MAT2A for metabolic reprogramming in non-small cell lung cancer cells","description":"These data are the original data from the manuscript entitled \"Integrating proteomics and metabolomics to reveal MAT2A for metabolic reprogramming in non-small cell lung cancer cells\". Below is a summary of the manuscript. Methionine adenosyltransferase 2A (MAT2A) links metabolic reprogramming with epigenetic regulation by generating S-adenosylmethionine (SAM) in the methionine cycle. The pattern of MAT2A regulation in metabolic reprogramming within non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) remains poorly understood. Current MAT2A inhibitors exhibit limited efficacy and additional therapeutic strategies need to be explored. Here, we employed proteomics and metabolomics in NSCLC cell lines treated with siRNA targeting MAT2A or the inhibitor AG-270, complemented by targeted metabolomics, RT-qPCR and ATAC-seq, to systematically characterize MAT2A-rewired metabolic reprogramming and identify potential combination strategies. Both MAT2A knockdown and inhibition significantly disrupt fatty acid biosynthesis, cholesterol metabolism, glycolysis and the transsulfuration pathway. In fatty acid biosynthesis, MAT2A influences the expression of key genes FASN and SCD and the levels of key metabolites palmitic acid (PA) and oleic acid (OA), as exogenous PA reverses the cell growth inhibition caused by AG-270. Furthermore, this metabolic link supports the rationale for combining AG-270 with the FASN inhibitor TVB-2640. In cholesterol metabolism, MAT2A regulates biosynthesis and efflux, and combining AG-270 with a liver X receptor agonist, which facilitates cholesterol efflux, augments anti-tumor efficacy. In energy metabolism, MAT2A influences glycolysis via regulation of HIF1A. The GLUT1 inhibitor which prevents glucose uptake, exhibits a synergetic effect when combined with AG-270. In the transsulfuration pathway, MAT2A transcriptionally regulates CBS, a key enzyme for cysteine biosynthesis. Combination treatments of AG-270 with inhibitors targeting genes upregulated in response to AG-270, such as PHGDH, which produces serine for cysteine biosynthesis, and SLC7A11, which mediates cysteine uptake, exhibit synergetic effects. Overall, our findings identify MAT2A as a critical regulator of metabolism in NSCLC and propose rational combination strategies to enhance MAT2A inhibitor efficacy.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-08-25T09:33:12.735Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fkbrcn84vz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fkbrcn84vz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"怡敏","last_name":"陈","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"84yybmrtxx","title":"Targeting riboswitches with synthetic small RNAs for metabolic engineering","description":"Raw data supporting the work \"Targeting riboswitches with synthetic small RNAs for metabolic engineering\". The data demonstrate the design and implementation of a new small RNA tool to target bacterial riboswitches. The synthetic sRNA activates gene expression at the transcription level by counteracting the riboswitch's control. The riboswitch-targeting sRNA is suitable for use in cell-free and cellular systems and can be combined into arrays for multiplex riboswitch-targeting.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-08-25T14:19:37.485Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/84yybmrtxx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/84yybmrtxx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Milca","last_name":"Lins","orcid":"0000-0003-2363-6768"},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Amorin","orcid":"0000-0002-6078-4412"},{"first_name":"Graciely","last_name":"Corrêa","orcid":"0000-0002-0005-096X"},{"first_name":"Bruno","last_name":"Picão","orcid":"0000-0001-7402-6826"},{"first_name":"Matthias","last_name":"Mack","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marcel","last_name":"Cerri","orcid":"0000-0001-6874-1313"},{"first_name":"Danielle","last_name":"Pedrolli","orcid":"0000-0002-3034-6497"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biotechnology","Synthetic Biology","Metabolic Engineering"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"yp7wt9cp3b","title":"western blot for LRTOR","description":"western blot raw data for \"Long non-coding RNA LRTOR drives resistance to osimertinib in non-small cell lung cancer by boosting the YAP positive feedback loop\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-09-04T13:20:49.769Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/yp7wt9cp3b","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/yp7wt9cp3b"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhimin","last_name":"Miao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fpnmx3f5tp","title":"Combined analysis of gut microbiome and serum metabolomics reveals novel biomarkers in patients with early-stage non-small cell lung cancer ","description":"early-stage non-small cell lung cancer serum metabolomics ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-12T13:35:16.013Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fpnmx3f5tp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fpnmx3f5tp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Boxiong","last_name":"Ni","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Lung Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nzrs6z3677","title":"Lung cancer cell derived exosomes enhance the metastasis of non-small cell lung cancer via SNHG12/miR-326/SLC7A11 axis","description":"The data are the raw data for the paper entitled \"Lung cancer cell derived exosomes enhance the metastasis of non-small cell lung cancer via SNHG12/miR-326/SLC7A11 axis\". ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-03-08T21:06:22.876Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nzrs6z3677","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nzrs6z3677"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rong","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Clinical Oncology","Experimental Oncology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vffmxyn7cy","title":"Original western blots","description":"The Original western blots of “Sappanchalcone Suppresses Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer Cells by Oxidative Stress-Driven DNA Damage and ER Stress Activation through PIEZO1 Modulation”","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-17T14:46:07.044Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vffmxyn7cy","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vffmxyn7cy"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"WeiYu","last_name":"Wu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wtmcww5csb","title":"The original dataset of the NSCLC project","description":"This dataset contains all the original data from the paper \"Lacticaseibacillus casei HG006